+# Drive with KiriGo: getting your KiriPay account ready
+
+KiriGo is the KiriPay delivery service. Drivers are paid straight into their KiriPay wallet, so every KiriGo driver needs a KiriPay account first, with their ID checked. This page walks you through it from the start. Most people finish in one sitting; the ID check then takes about a day.
+
+> You'll need: a phone with a camera, an email address, your **passport or driver's licence**, and — if you'll drive a motorbike, car, van or truck — your **driver's licence**.
+
+## 1. Get KiriPay and create your account
+
+Install KiriPay from the [download page](/download), or open **kiripay.online** in your browser. Tap **Create an account** and enter your name exactly as it is on your ID, your email, your mobile number and a password.
+
+## 2. Confirm your email or mobile number
+
+Open the email from KiriPay and tap the confirm link (or confirm your mobile number with the 6-digit text). Until you do, KiriPay can't send, pay or check your ID.
+
+## 3. Get your ID checked (Level 2)
+
+This is the step KiriGo needs. In KiriPay open **Verify your account**, then choose **Level 2: your ID**.
+
+1. Choose your document: **Passport** or **Driving licence**. If you'll drive a motor vehicle, use your driver's licence — KiriGo checks it anyway, so one document does both jobs.
+2. Type your full name, document number, date of birth and expiry date exactly as they appear on the document.
+3. Take a clear photo of the document: the passport photo page, or the front of the licence (and the back too if it has anything written on it).
+4. Take a selfie: face the camera, in good light, no hat or sunglasses.
+5. Tap **Send**. You'll get an email when it has been checked, usually within a day.
+
+Your document must not be expired. If it comes back **Not approved**, the reason is shown on the same page — fix it and send again.
+
+## 4. Turn on two-step sign-in
+
+Drivers receive money, so KiriGo asks for the extra lock. Install an authenticator app (Google Authenticator, Microsoft Authenticator, Authy or 1Password). In KiriPay open **Security → Two-step sign-in → Set up two-step sign-in**, scan the code with the authenticator app, and type the 6-digit number it shows. Save your recovery codes somewhere safe.
+
+## 5. Set an app PIN
+
+While you're in **Security**, set a 4 to 6 digit **App PIN**. KiriPay then asks for it whenever it opens, so nobody else can use your wallet if your phone is lost.
+
+## 6. Sign up on KiriGo
+
+Once your ID shows **Approved**, go to **[kirigo.online/driver](https://kirigo.online/driver/)** and tap **Sign in with KiriPay**. KiriGo never sees your password. Then fill in:
+
+- your first name (customers see this),
+- your vehicle and plate number, with a photo showing the plate,
+- a photo of your driver's licence (for any motor vehicle),
+- your prices: a base fee, a price per km, and your minimum charge.
+
+An admin checks that your licence matches the photo on your KiriPay ID. When you're approved you get a driver number like **KG-0142** and can go online. Each time you go online, KiriGo asks for a quick selfie so nobody else can drive on your account.
+
+## Getting paid
+
+You keep **100% of every delivery charge**. It lands in your KiriPay wallet the moment you hand an order over and the customer's code is scanned. Cash it out to your bank like any other KiriPay money, from **Top up or cash out**. KiriGo charges a small monthly fee from your wallet; the first 3 months are free.
+
+## If something is stuck
+
+| What you see | What to do |
+|---|---|
+| KiriGo says your ID needs to be approved | Finish step 3 and wait for the approval email, then sign in to KiriGo again. |
+| KiriGo asks for two-step sign-in | Finish step 4, then sign in to KiriGo again. |
+| Your ID came back Not approved | Read the reason on **Verify your account**, retake the photo or fix the details, and send again. |
+| You can't confirm your email | Check your spam folder, or confirm your mobile number instead. |
+| Anything else | Open **Support** in KiriPay and send us a message. |
